DESCRIPTION:Something strange and unusual is coming to Mary Collins at Che
 rry Valley School! The school's Theater Arts Program (TAP) presents *Beetl
 ejuice JR.*\, running October 30–November 8\, 2026\, featuring two casts
  of talented young performers and a student technical crew bringing the be
 loved Broadway musical to life.\n\nUnder the leadership of Darby Ciampi\, 
 Lindsey Nettleton\, and an experienced creative team\, TAP delivers an amb
 itious theatrical experience that goes far beyond the stage. Students are 
 involved in every aspect of production\, from acting\, singing\, and chore
 ography to lighting\, sound\, set construction\, costumes\, and props. Wit
 h professional mentorship\, students gain hands-on experience in the full 
 theatrical process\, developing creativity\, confidence\, and collaboratio
 n along the way.
