BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DOMESTICATED by Patrick Atkinson - an original play reading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
UID:261027taDU99zFU0eKj6H97S3yMA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a staged reading of DOMESTICATED\, an original pla
 y by Patrick Atkinson\, presented by Bay Area Stage Productions. Experienc
 e a new work in an intimate setting where story\, language\, and performan
 ce take center stage.\n\nDomesticated tells the story of four pets living 
 in a remote house in the country. Suddenly alone with no one to take care 
 of them\, they must find a way to survive. Along the way\, they remember t
 heir lives with each other. It is a story of the joys and sorrows of livin
 g together\, of how we remember and honor the friends we lose\, and of the
  will to go on.\n\nCast: Maya Rath as Annie\, Jessica Schild as Tina\, Isa
 ac Arriaga as Bob\, Ginger Burnett as Suzette\, Bill Chessman as Dave\, Su
 zan Lorraine as Chloe\, Amanda Beaton as Ensemble
LOCATION:Bay Area Stage Theatre
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/domesticated-by-patrick-atkinson
 -an-original-play-reading
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bird of Prey Hike at Lynch Canyon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
UID:261027bQv25LrYE0SiKExTbghuTQ
DESCRIPTION:Each year from fall through late winter West County Hawkwatch 
 leads weekend hikes so people can learn about the birds of prey that call 
 the Solano Land Trust properties their home.\n\nDuring this viewing season
 \, bring your binoculars and join a group to see the magnificent bids that
  rely on our protected agricultural open spaces for habitat. Birders of al
 l levels of experience are welcome.\n\nFor a complete schedule of West Cou
 nty Hawkwatch events\, visit the group’s website at: westcountyhawkwatch
 .com or its Facebook page.
LOCATION:Lynch Canyon Open Space
URL:https://solanolandtrust.org/events-news/event-calendar.html/event/2026
