BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T210000
UID:261026sPNpJL3gxEqmXi-8qEO8AQ
DESCRIPTION:Dia de los Muertos \\(Day of the Dead\\) is a Latin American t
 radition\, where we can all meet and remember our ancestors. Come experien
 ce the traditions of\, art\, music\, Catrinas\, and beautiful ofrendas as 
 we gather in love and remembrance. Bring a photograph of a loved one who h
 as passed and place it on our Community Altar/Ofrenda. Together\, let’s 
 create a place where memories\, cultures\, and hearts come together.\n\nIf
  you knew Calvin Ellington come\, share your memories with Mario. If you n
 ever had the chance to meet Calvin\, join us in celebrating love and the l
 asting mark our loved ones leave on our lives.
LOCATION:Downtown Vallejo
URL:https://www.facebook.com/JoinSolanoAIDSCoalition/posts/pfbid0WDGcTV2iQ
 k9wW3FovyYvVWa1XeBDsMkRZ1QTP83xik4YXih3mzY4RHjLmkuMPxBml
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mary Collins School at Cherry Valley Presents Beetlejuice JR
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
UID:261026UEhylHhxqECOtkjO7Jx4XA
DESCRIPTION:Something strange and unusual is coming to Mary Collins at Che
 rry Valley School! The school's Theater Arts Program (TAP) presents *Beetl
 ejuice JR.*\, running October 30–November 8\, 2026\, featuring two casts
  of talented young performers and a student technical crew bringing the be
 loved Broadway musical to life.\n\nUnder the leadership of Darby Ciampi\, 
 Lindsey Nettleton\, and an experienced creative team\, TAP delivers an amb
 itious theatrical experience that goes far beyond the stage. Students are 
 involved in every aspect of production\, from acting\, singing\, and chore
 ography to lighting\, sound\, set construction\, costumes\, and props. Wit
 h professional mentorship\, students gain hands-on experience in the full 
 theatrical process\, developing creativity\, confidence\, and collaboratio
 n along the way.
LOCATION:Mary Collins School at Cherry Vallet
URL:https://my.cheddarup.com/c/mccv-beetlejuice-jr/items
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Dia de Muertos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T210000
UID:261024_sJ17P_phUaDNNWdVM07Bg
DESCRIPTION:November 1\, 2026 at 6 PM\n\nThe Sonoma Community Center will 
 hold its 17th annual Día de Muertos altar lighting on November 1 at 6
 :30 PM at the west side of the SCC Front Garden\, followed by a celebratio
 n with traditional Ballet Folklórico dancers\, food vendors and cultura
 l activities on the SCC Back Patio. Whether they were family\, a dear frie
 nd\, a beloved companion\, or someone whose life touched yours\, their mem
 ory has a place here.  One may also write a personal message on one of t
 he gold paper butterflies provided at the altar\, and hang it alongside t
 he images.\n\nSchedule of Events\n\n6:30 PM – Lighting of the Altar\n\n7
 :00 PM – Performance by Grupo Folklórico Quetzalen Sonoma\n\n7:30 PM 
 – Food will be available\n\nAll Night – Free Face painting for adults 
 & children\n\nAbout the Altar\n\nOur 12’ public altar\, constructed by l
 ocal sculptor Jim Callahan\, has ample room for photos and other items tha
 t honor lost loved ones\, and every year we invite community members to co
 ntribute their mementos to the ofrenda in a shared celebration of those wh
 o have passed on. See how to submit a photo below. Community members are w
 armly invited to bring a weather-resistant photograph or image of a depar
 ted loved one and hang it on the altar starting Friday\, October 25th.\n\
 nDia Programming & Classes\n\nEvery October\, the Center offers a variety 
 of programs and other activities in conjunction with Día de Muertos\, inv
 iting our community to join us in exploring the cultural practices and tra
 ditions surrounding this holiday. Please check our event calendar for more
  information about upcoming Día de Muertos programming and events.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/events-galleries/dia-de-muertos/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de los Muertos: Meet the Artists & Altaristas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T150000
UID:261024BKeE8AUo0k-MXzeWcrlAUQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Museum of Sonoma County for a special opportuni
 ty to connect with the local artists and altaristas featured in our 30th A
 nnual Día de los Muertos exhibition. Throughout the hour\, participating 
 artists and altaristas will share brief gallery talks about their work\, c
 reative processes\, and the stories and traditions behind their offerings.
  Visitors are also invited to chat with the artists\, ask questions\, and 
 learn more about the personal meaning and cultural significance of this an
 nual exhibition.
LOCATION:Museums of Sonoma County
URL:https://tickets.museumsc.org/?tab=Events&view_date=&period=Weekly&mode
 =Event&event=1792606579909x585753233323458600
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Day of the Dead multi day altar exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180000
UID:261023Kpp793OeZk6wwrbXciJFnA
DESCRIPTION:Oct. 26 - Nov. 2  Día de los Muertos ALTARS EXHIBITION \\(5-
 8pm weeknights.\\)\n\nOct. 31\, Saturday altar exhibition \\(extended hour
 s\, 10am-3pm\\)\n\nNov. 1 Día de los Muertos CELEBRATION \\(1pm -6pm\\) s
 tarts with a Nahua indigenous Mexican blessing\, includes ballet folkorico
  and danzante groups\, live music\, traditional foods\, art activities & f
 ace painting. \\(Food is for sale.\\)
LOCATION:Napa Valley Center for Spiritual Living
URL:https://www.napacountyhispanicnetwork.org/latinoheritagecommittee
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
