BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Drawing Portraits From Photos (3 Session Class)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T210000
UID:261023BuMH_qgXhU6n8uu5JiH0jg
DESCRIPTION:**Introduction to Drawing Portraits from Photos** \n\n*Novembe
 r 4th\, 11th\, and 18th* \n\n*6:00-9:00pm* \n\n*$150.00 + $15.00 Materials
  Fee = $165.00* \n\n*Age Restricted to 18+* \n\n**About this class:** \n\n
 In this three week course\, students will learn and practice observational
  skills and fundamental drawing techniques while learning the basics of dr
 awing portraits from photographs. \n\nDrawing human faces requires the sa
 me basic drawing skills that one employs for any subject - observing propo
 rtion\, flattening shapes\, and utilizing line or value to convey volume. 
 But the conceptual weight of human faces tends to intimidate artists. When
  drawing any subject\, the hardest skill is simply learning to see\, a ski
 ll that anyone can be taught\, practice\, and hone. This course will focus
  on the practice of looking\, and discovering strategies to find objectivi
 ty when rendering portraits. \n\nThis class is for anyone who wants to pr
 actice and advance their drawing skills - beginners\, those who haven’t 
 practiced in years\, or any artists who just want to learn new techniques 
 and practice their skills with consistent feedback and guidance. Through d
 emonstration\, practice\, and reflective discussion\, this class will expl
 ore the foundations of rendering human expression with classical drawing t
 echniques in a low pressure environment. \n\nObservational drawing gives 
 all artists a foundation of practical knowledge and skills that infinitely
  expands the possibilities of what one can create. If your ideas feel limi
 ted by your drawing skills\, if you feel frustrated or stuck in your paint
 ing practice\, or if you simply want to start drawing and are looking for 
 a place to start\, this is the class for you.\n\n***About the Instructor:*
 ** *Hannah Day received her BA in Visual Arts with an emphasis on drawing 
 and printmaking from University of San Diego\, then attended University of
  Hawaii at Manoa to receive her MFA in printmaking. Hannah’s etchings ha
 ve been internationally shown and collected\, but her art practice also in
 cludes paper cutting\, graphite\, and watercolor. She has taught all ages 
 in many mediums. These days\, Hannah primarily teaches watercolor\, observ
 ational drawing\, and paper cutting. You can view her work at www.hannahdr
 awstrees.com*
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classeslectures/p/drawingportraitsfromphotos
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
