SUMMARY:Bottega Cellar Series with Marchesi Antinori
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T210000
UID:261006vmGI3cV5JkyYQ2fPloh1Xg
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bottega on November 4th for an elegant evening feat
 uring Marchesi Antinori\, hosted by Estate Manager Glenn Salva. Marchesi A
 ntinori is a historic Tuscan winemaking family that helped pioneer the Sup
 er Tuscan movement. With a winemaking legacy dating back to 1385 and conti
 nuous family ownership\, the business is now led by the 26th generation wh
 o continue to guide Marchesi Antinori's tradition of bold innovation balan
 ced with deep respect for heritage and the land. The dinner will feature a
  selection of wines from the Antinori portfolio\, including Tignanello and
  Guado al Tasso. Guests will experience a thoughtfully curated progression
  of wines from one of Italy’s most storied wine families\, paired with a
  seasonal multi-course menu by Bottega Executive Chef Alex Espinoza. Each 
 course is designed to complement the character and expression of the wines
 \, bringing together refined flavors\, exceptional ingredients\, and the g
 racious hospitality that defines Bottega. Price is inclusive of tax and gr
 atuity.\n\n6525 Washington Street Suite A9\, Yountville\, CA 94599\n\n(707
 ) 945-1050
LOCATION:Bottega Napa Valley
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=25489&r
 estref=25489&experienceId=791062&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&u
 tm_campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T170000
UID:260930ybU_EpEpZU63LXwivtNGag
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
