DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T113000
UID:260903bfX0C-EIZUWMk12zlQc15Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this free educational seminar open to all Sonoma C
 ounty employers\, business leaders\, HR professionals\, and managers. The 
 final session of this three-part Workplace & Workforce Innovation series f
 ocuses on workplace practices that help organizations recruit\, retain\, a
 nd support talented employees. Presented by employment law attorney Samant
 ha Pungprakearti\, this seminar explores legal requirements alongside prac
 tical\, affordable strategies that create a more supportive workplace cult
 ure and strengthen your competitive advantage as an employer. Participants
  will learn: Employer responsibilities for providing lactation accommodati
 ons and creating compliant\, supportive workplaces for nursing employees. 
 How employee benefits\, compensation options\, and family-friendly policie
 s can help attract and retain top talent. Free or inexpensive\, high-impac
 t family-friendly practices for tighter budgets that improve employee sati
 sfaction\, strengthen retention\, and position organizations as employers 
 of choice. The FREE series is presented by the Santa Rosa Metro Chamber as
  part of its Workplace & Workforce Innovation initiative\, helping employe
 rs build workplaces where employees and businesses thrive. This free serie
 s is made possible through funding from First 5 Sonoma County and Measure 
 I.
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Dowtown Square
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1452329726705760/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Supervisor Cassandra James Community Engagement Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T193000
UID:2610277l1yYqvtNU2kizOOX0W8xg
DESCRIPTION:This is an opportunity to listen\, learn\, and build community
  together. Your voice matters\, and we want to hear from you!\n\nSolano Co
 unty Supervisor Cassandra James\, Vallejo Council Member Helen-Marie Gordo
