BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michelle Lambert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
UID:261012TL_aaXk1WkqHHwxAEUiu-Q
DESCRIPTION:Join Michelle at JaM Cellars in downtown Napa for an evening s
 how. More info available here: https://jamcellars.com/\n\nBay Area breakou
 t artist Michelle Lambert delivers a fun\, high-energy show filled with ed
 gy\, heartfelt original music\, infectious pop hooks\, and unstoppable cha
 risma. Fresh off a successful 40-date tour across the Western states last 
 year\, Michelle captivates audiences with soaring vocals\, dynamic violin 
 solos\, and vibrant energy that radiates through the crowd. Her electrifyi
 ng performances create an unforgettable live experience that will have you
  dancing\, smiling\, and celebrating all night long.\n\nRaised in Northern
  California and trained at the prestigious Berklee College of Music\, Mich
 elle Lambert has forged her own path as a fearless\, independent pop artis
 t. She has topped the charts of Indie Radio with her original songs and wa
 s featured in the San Francisco Giants’ City Connect Campaign as a notab
 le Bay Area artist. Michelle cut her teeth performing and writing in the c
 ompetitive music scenes of Nashville and Los Angeles before returning to t
 he Bay Area to tour with her own thriving career. Known for her powerful v
 ocals\, masterful violin playing\, and bold\, colorful costumes\, Michelle
  pairs striking visuals with raw emotional storytelling—embodying creati
 vity\, resilience\, and the adventure of chasing your dreams. For more inf
 o on Michelle visit: https://www.michellelambert.com
LOCATION:JaM Cellars
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108834608?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa Beginner - 4-Week Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
UID:261003iWcPMQGNqUKgLYKCLZjCKQ
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nNovember 5- November 26\n\nClass requires a minimum of 8 reg
 istrations to run. Please register soon so we can secure the session!\n\nT
 his is a beginner cuban salsa—you will learn your basic footwork and tur
 ns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn the fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, in
 cluding body movement\, rhythm\, musicality\, footwork\, partner connectio
 n\, and partnerwork patterns inspired by authentic Cuban dance culture. We
  focus on proper technique\, coordination\, flow\, and natural body expres
 sion\, while also building confidence and strong foundations.\n\nClasses a
 re structured with:\n\n• Warm-up and body movement\n\n• Footwork and r
 hythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork technique\n\n• Short combinations and
  practical applications\n\nOur goal is to help you understand how to dance
  salsa\, not just memorize steps — developing timing\, connection\, and 
 a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing.\n\nCome dance with us\, grow your t
 echnique\, and experience the energy and flavor of Cuba in a supportive an
 d welcoming environment.\n\nBook your spot\n\nDate & Time:\n\n4week class\
 , November 5- November 26\n\nThursdays @ 7:30 PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood 
 Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor m
 arking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T170000
UID:260930tzaobJSu2USUPhfdoXzvkA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
