DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T163000
UID:260909TjFURTO4lEC_HvDaJgD3yA
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T160000
UID:260909DQERHzkJxEa-hM2iBtC5Bw
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
UID:260415Sy0X6Kz0EkuPCsMJeTHJxA
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Primary Care Conference November 4-8\, 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T170000
UID:2511260mo6fFRzcE-dFcsPip1ajw
DESCRIPTION:The Napa Primary Care Conference is a unique educational confe
 rence for physicians and medical professionals who care for active and ath
 letic patients or who themselves lead such a lifestyle.\n\n16 HOURS AAFP C
 ME CREDIT\n\nLocation\n\nThe conference will be held at The Napa Valley Ma
 rriott Resort and Spa\, conveniently located within minutes of renowned wi
 neries\, shopping\, attractions\, and numerous options for exercise and ph
 ysical activity.\n\nCourse Description\n\nThis conference will present ver
 y practical information that you can use in your practice. Topics will inc
 lude common medical and musculoskeletal problems that affect patients who 
 lead an active lifestyle. The focus will be on providing information that 
 will help you diagnose and manage these conditions in the office\; so that
  you can help your patients get moving again and improve their performance
 . In addition\, various topics on healthy lifestyles and personal wellness
  will make this conference a valuable experience for all attendees.\n\nInt
 ended Audience\n\nThe curriculum is directed to Family Medicine\, Internal
  Medicine\, Pediatrics\, Emergency Medicine\, PM and R and Orthopedics spe
 cialists as well as Physical Therapists\, Athletic Trainers\, Physicians A
 ssistants\, Nurse Practitioners and others who want to earn Continuing Med
 ical Education from leading physician experts who are outstanding speakers
 .\n\nCourse Learning Objectives\n\nUpon conclusion of this program\, parti
 cipants should be able to:\n\n1. Describe recent advances regarding variou
 s medical problems and their impact on the athlete and exercise performanc
 e.\n\n2. Identify current recommendations for proper nutrition in active a
 nd athletic patients.\n\n3. Illustrate key skills in the diagnosis and man
 agement of common musculoskeletal problems encountered by family physician
 s.\n\n4. Diagnose common problems encountered by patients and effectively 
 treat these conditions.\n\n5. Define common medical-legal issues relevant 
 to the primary care physician.\n\nWe hope you can join us for this unique 
 conference in 2024. I look forward to meeting you in Napa!\n\nSincerely\,\
 n\nRobert Sallis\, MD\, FACSM\, FAAFP\n\nConference Chairman\n\nFamily Med
 icine Physician\n\nClinical Professor of Family Medicine\n\nUC Riverside S
 chool of Medicine\n\nDepartment of Family Medicine\n\nKaiser Permanente Me
 dical Center\, Fontana\, CA\n\nFacebook: https://go.evvnt.com/3362322-2?pi
 d=6630\n\nDate and Time: On Wed\, 04 Nov 2026 16:00 - Sun\, 08 Nov 2026 10
 :00\n\nSpeakers: Robert Sallis\, MD Clinical Professor of Family Medicine 
 Kaiser Permanente Bernard J Tyson School of Medicine UC Riverside School o
 f Medicine Chief Medical Officer Los Angeles Football Club Lead Primary Ca
 re Physician Los Angeles Clippers Program Director Emerituis Sports Medici
 ne Fellowship Kaiser Permanente Medical Center Fontana\, CA \, Columbus D 
 Batiste\, MD\, FACC\, FSCAI\, John DiFiori\, MD\, FACSM\, FAMSSM Director 
 of Sports Medicine National Basketball Association\, Neel Doshi\, DO Child
 \, Adolescent\, and Adult Psychiatrist Assistant Chief\, Department of Psy
 chiatry Associate Professor\, Kaiser Permanente Family Medicine Residency 
 Program Kaiser Permanente Orange County\, Jessie Roberts Fudge\, MD FACSM 
 Sports Medicine Physician Kaiser Permanente\, Everett WA Special Olympics 
 Washington Board of Directors Global Medical Advisor\, Special Olympics In
 ternational\, Greg Maletis\, MD Chief of Orthopedic Surgery Kaiser Permane
 nte\, Baldwin Park Lead Physician\; Kaiser ACL Registry Clinical Professor
  of Orthopedics Keck School of Medicine of USC
LOCATION:Napa Valley Marriott Hotel
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/napa-primary-care-confe
 rence-november-4-8-2026/17504571/2026-11-05T16
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
