BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lost Canadians\, Border Crossings\, and Citizenship by Descent (Sp
 eaker Series)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T133000
UID:261022NE2yjsgry0OYHicI41a1yg
DESCRIPTION:Kathryn Lake Hogan Hailing from Southwestern Ontario\, Kathryn
 's lineage includes a mixture of Canadian\, Loyalist and New England branc
 hes and roots connecting her to England and Wales. But her passion doesn't
  stop at her own genealogy\; Kathryn's mission is to help others discover 
 their Canadian ancestral connections. Kathryn's dynamic presentations\, ra
 nging from society meetings to genealogical research institutes in Canada 
 and the United States\, have earned her a reputation as one of the leading
  voices in Canadian genealogy. Whether you've attended one of her sessions
  or tuned into her "Genealogy with a Canadian Twist" webinars\, you've lik
 ely felt the excitement of Kathryn's dedication. Kathryn's commitment goes
  beyond her business. She believes in nurturing and growing the genealogy 
 community. Having served in leadership roles for notable organizations suc
 h as Ontario Ancestors\, the Association of Professional Genealogists\, an
 d the United Empire Loyalists Association of Canada\, she continues to cha
 mpion greater accessibility\, inclusivity\, and diversity in family histor
 y.  GSVB Members will automatically receive a Zoom invitation that will be
  sent out a couple of days before the meeting.  Non-Members: If you are in
 terested in attending\, please send an e-mail to GSVBzoom@gmail.com GSVBzo
 om@gmail.com to request a Zoom invitation. The Zoom meeting time is at 1:3
 0 pm Pacific Time. The event is FREE. All are welcome. More information on
  the event can be found on the Genealogy Society of Vallejo-Benicia's webs
 ite at  www.gsvb.org  and Facebook page at  www.facebook.com/GSVB.org
LOCATION:Via Zoom
URL:https://gsvb.org/eventListings.php?nm=34
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T170000
UID:260430zlvTskRaGUSGL_b7XHzavQ
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
