DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T180000
UID:261014TVy5MjWhuE60CN2bPKtn1g
DESCRIPTION:San Ramon’s Poet Laureate Jaz Sufi filters her slam-honed in
 tensity through queer Iranian-American identity to spin you with spellbind
 ing storytelling.\n\nFound Poets! is about the entertainment of the spirit
  through performance poetry. From our development program grads to nationa
 lly acclaimed headliners\, Found Poets! is a challenging\, committed poetr
 y community dedicated to hosting a good night out.\n\n(Headliner)\n\n**Jaz
  Sufi**\n\nJaz Sufi (she/hers) is a queer Iranian-American poet and arts e
 ducator. She is the author of *Catalog of Shadows* (Game Over Books). Her 
 work has been published in Best New Poets\, Best of the Net\, AGNI\, Black
  Warrior Review\, Muzzle\, and elsewhere. She is a National Poetry Slam fi
 nalist and has received fellowships from Kundiman\, the Watering Hole\, an
 d New York University\, where she received her MFA. She is the current Poe
 t Laureate of San Ramon on occupied Ohlone land\, where she lives with her
  dog\, Apollo. IG: @calamityjaz www.jazsufi.com\n\n(Openers)\n\n**Grayson 
 Thompson**\n\nGrayson Thompson \\[he/him\\]\, a Black\, Jamaican-American\
 , queer transgender poet and therapist\, won Foglifter Press’s 2024 Star
 t A Riot! Chapbook Prize (June 2025) and Write Bloody Publishing’s 2024 
 Jack McCarthy Book Prize (September 2025) for *Sand Bodied Florida Boy.* I
 G: @graysonwritespoems www.graysonwritespoems.com\n\n**Ernesto Garay**\n\n
 Ernesto M. Garay is the author of a poetry collection\, *Reverberating Voi
 ces* (Flowersong Press\, 2022). Garay was LA Revista Bilingüe: La Voz’s
  Person of the Month in Sonoma County for March 2020\, and a Sonoma County
  Discovered Award Recipient in Literary Arts. He is Ethnic Studies faculty
  at Sierra College.\n\n**Anika Snyder**\n\nAnika Snyder was born and raise
 d in Northern California. She published her first book\, *Syllable Soccer*
 \, in 2025 and is soon to release her second. She has been published in Ef
 fable Press and performs her work regularly around Mendocino and Sonoma co
 unties. IG: @anika366\n\n**Gary Weiner**\n\nGary Weiner moved to Sonoma Co
 unty in 1973 and now resides in Sebastopol. A former working musician and 
 lawyer\, he released the full-length album *Released at Last* featuring N
 ina Gerber and exhibits photography in galleries across San Francisco and 
 Sebastopol. He is a prolific writer featured by the Sebastopol Center for 
 the Arts. IG: @gaweiner https://www.garyweinerarts.com/\n\n**Hosted by Jos
 h Windmiller + Original Giotis!**
LOCATION:The Big Easy
URL:https://foundpoets.org/events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
