BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Primary Care Conference November 4-8\, 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:251126UaacAusQ0U21kGFlxBqiCQ
DESCRIPTION:The Napa Primary Care Conference is a unique educational confe
 rence for physicians and medical professionals who care for active and ath
 letic patients or who themselves lead such a lifestyle.\n\n16 HOURS AAFP C
 ME CREDIT\n\nLocation\n\nThe conference will be held at The Napa Valley Ma
 rriott Resort and Spa\, conveniently located within minutes of renowned wi
 neries\, shopping\, attractions\, and numerous options for exercise and ph
 ysical activity.\n\nCourse Description\n\nThis conference will present ver
 y practical information that you can use in your practice. Topics will inc
 lude common medical and musculoskeletal problems that affect patients who 
 lead an active lifestyle. The focus will be on providing information that 
 will help you diagnose and manage these conditions in the office\; so that
  you can help your patients get moving again and improve their performance
 . In addition\, various topics on healthy lifestyles and personal wellness
  will make this conference a valuable experience for all attendees.\n\nInt
 ended Audience\n\nThe curriculum is directed to Family Medicine\, Internal
  Medicine\, Pediatrics\, Emergency Medicine\, PM and R and Orthopedics spe
 cialists as well as Physical Therapists\, Athletic Trainers\, Physicians A
 ssistants\, Nurse Practitioners and others who want to earn Continuing Med
 ical Education from leading physician experts who are outstanding speakers
 .\n\nCourse Learning Objectives\n\nUpon conclusion of this program\, parti
 cipants should be able to:\n\n1. Describe recent advances regarding variou
 s medical problems and their impact on the athlete and exercise performanc
 e.\n\n2. Identify current recommendations for proper nutrition in active a
 nd athletic patients.\n\n3. Illustrate key skills in the diagnosis and man
 agement of common musculoskeletal problems encountered by family physician
 s.\n\n4. Diagnose common problems encountered by patients and effectively 
 treat these conditions.\n\n5. Define common medical-legal issues relevant 
 to the primary care physician.\n\nWe hope you can join us for this unique 
 conference in 2024. I look forward to meeting you in Napa!\n\nSincerely\,\
 n\nRobert Sallis\, MD\, FACSM\, FAAFP\n\nConference Chairman\n\nFamily Med
 icine Physician\n\nClinical Professor of Family Medicine\n\nUC Riverside S
 chool of Medicine\n\nDepartment of Family Medicine\n\nKaiser Permanente Me
 dical Center\, Fontana\, CA\n\nFacebook: https://go.evvnt.com/3362322-2?pi
 d=6630\n\nDate and Time: On Wed\, 04 Nov 2026 16:00 - Sun\, 08 Nov 2026 10
 :00\n\nSpeakers: Robert Sallis\, MD Clinical Professor of Family Medicine 
 Kaiser Permanente Bernard J Tyson School of Medicine UC Riverside School o
 f Medicine Chief Medical Officer Los Angeles Football Club Lead Primary Ca
 re Physician Los Angeles Clippers Program Director Emerituis Sports Medici
 ne Fellowship Kaiser Permanente Medical Center Fontana\, CA \, Columbus D 
 Batiste\, MD\, FACC\, FSCAI\, John DiFiori\, MD\, FACSM\, FAMSSM Director 
 of Sports Medicine National Basketball Association\, Neel Doshi\, DO Child
 \, Adolescent\, and Adult Psychiatrist Assistant Chief\, Department of Psy
 chiatry Associate Professor\, Kaiser Permanente Family Medicine Residency 
 Program Kaiser Permanente Orange County\, Jessie Roberts Fudge\, MD FACSM 
 Sports Medicine Physician Kaiser Permanente\, Everett WA Special Olympics 
 Washington Board of Directors Global Medical Advisor\, Special Olympics In
 ternational\, Greg Maletis\, MD Chief of Orthopedic Surgery Kaiser Permane
 nte\, Baldwin Park Lead Physician\; Kaiser ACL Registry Clinical Professor
  of Orthopedics Keck School of Medicine of USC
LOCATION:Napa Valley Marriott Hotel
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/napa-primary-care-confe
 rence-november-4-8-2026/17504571/2026-11-07T16
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
