BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T170000
UID:261028c6BCLsSlgE23dfiJHHTxiQ
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STIMULANT: Art as Remedy for Diseased Culture\, Exhibition and Eve
 nts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T160000
UID:261021pi7NidSumk-NsJ4NSXDx-w
DESCRIPTION:In a diseased society with failing systems\, what can we do to
  turn things around? For two weeks a new exhibition from Sonoma County’s
  own Apocalypse Studio\, a father and daughter artist duo\, *STIMULANT: A
 rt as Remedy for Diseased Culture* proposes that art is the antidote and 
 creativity is the countermove. This exhibition explores the inner and oute
 r work of co-creating that antidote: art that stimulates society’s creat
 ivity - the social sculpture we all create together. There will be two per
 formances\, two lectures\, a Parisian -style Art Salon\, and times to visi
 t the large exhibition and talk with the artists. All events are free to 
 attend. Visit www.apocalypse.art/stimulant for details and schedule of eve
 nts.
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Endless Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T180000
UID:261014EGDas0tYskGyom3neGSxng
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  10/12/26\n\n**NOVEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 ENDLESS INSPIRATION**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– October 26  – November 22\
 , 2026**\n\n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, November 7\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to
  meet Ron Sumner and Karen Miller and learn about their art and inspiratio
 n.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a 
 beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSo
 noma County artist\, **Ron Sumner\,** presents **Endless Inspiration**\, a
  collection of new paintings and classic works that highlight his lifelong
  love of nature featuring landscapes\, animals and wildlife\, with a speci
 al focus on birds.  The essence of this golden state shines forth in “C
 alifornia Hills\,” a large oil painting of a sweep of oak covered hills.
    Turning to wildlife\, Sumner’s masterful watercolor rendition in th
 e “Young Fox” captures its wild nature on stark alert.  And the compe
 lling presence of a most majestic bird is beautifully memorialized in his 
 “Blue Heron” watercolor.  Other birds depicted in his works include p
 arrots\, penguins and owls.  “In my painting\, I always strive to trans
 late my emotional response to the world of nature around us – to share t
 his deep feeling with those who view my work\,” commented Sumner on his 
 inspiration.\n\nA lifelong Northern Californian\, Sumner began his art tra
 ining in school.  After earning a BFA from the California College of Arts
  & Crafts\, he was a technical illustrator for a number of years before tr
 ansitioning to a full-time fine arts painter.  With an emphasis in waterc
 olor\, he has won numerous awards\, including Best of Show at the Society 
 of Western Artists.  His portrait of John F. Kennedy is part of the perma
 nent collection at the John F. Kennedy Library.  He has exhibited widely 
 and was part of the Veterans Art Show for CA vets in 2023.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Sumner will co-host Art Nite on 11/5 from 5 pm to 7 pm.\n\nThe Stairw
 ay Smallworks Showcase features **Karen Miller’**s **Historic Gems\,** f
 eaturing pastel paintings that honor our history – local artifacts that 
 are disappearing.  Highlighting this exhibit\, “Ghost Bridge\,” an ea
 rly 20th century railroad bridge known as Healdsburg Railroad Bridge is so
 on to give way for the Smart Train.  Its unique style is a key element to
  our local character but sadly could not be upgraded for modern rail.  Fr
 om old trucks to a beloved schoolhouse\, these paintings harken fond memor
 ies.  Part of our world for years\, they enriched our lives and are not t
 o be forgotten.  Noted Miller on the impetus for her series\, “I want t
 o catch old things before they’re gone – memorializing those things cl
 ose to our hearts.”\n\nMeet the artist: Miller will host the Gallery on 
 October 26 and November 2\, 11\, 14 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n Also j
 oin us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, November 5\, 5 – 7 pm. 
  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a communi
 ty event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participati
 ng.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\,
  Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    
 **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beve
 rly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freestyle Playground Dance Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T193000
UID:261008JXjAvh7fpEa-wngJl_a-vQ
DESCRIPTION:Freestyle Playground — 4-Week Dance & Movement Series\n\nExp
 lore. Play. Create. Express.\n\nReady to discover new ways of moving and e
 xpressing yourself through dance?\n\nFreestyle Playground is a playful\, c
 reative dance class designed to expand your movement vocabulary\, spark yo
 ur imagination\, and help you discover your own unique movement style.\n\n
 Through guided freestyle exercises\, imaginative movement concepts\, music
 ality\, elements of popping\, rhythm\, and body awareness\, you'll explore
  new ways to move\, experiment\, and create.\n\nEach week\, we'll introduc
 e different movement tools and concepts that you can combine\, build upon\
 , and incorporate into your own dancing.\n\nThis isn't a choreography-base
 d class. It's about exploration\, curiosity\, and the freedom to move with
 out worrying about getting it "right."\n\nWhether you're an experienced da
 ncer looking for fresh inspiration or someone curious about exploring move
 ment\, all levels are welcome!\n\nClass Details\n\n📍 Laguna Lab | Sebas
 topol\, CA\n\n📅 4 Tuesdays: October 27\, November 3\, 10 & 17\n\n⏰ 6:
 30–7:30 PM\n\n💃 All levels welcome!\n\nCome expand your creativity\, 
 discover new movement possibilities\, and experience the joy of freestyle 
 dance!\n\nNo perfection. Just movement\, music\, imagination & PLAY!
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://www.tickettailor.com/events/lagunalab/2417443
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
