BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T170000
UID:260430ya_9xq7eZECexQzWemEMGg
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Feminist Book Club: Shut Up\, This Is Serious by Carolina Ixta
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T183000
UID:261021tn3ew-S4k0Kkb43kbTZu8A
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an online discussion! The Feminist Book Club meets
  monthly to discuss books exploring feminist issues. Selections for the cl
 ub span literature\, memoir\, graphic novels\, essay collections and works
  of nonfiction. Hosted by Jenna Sanders and Stephanie Der\, the Feminist B
 ook Club is open to people and their experiences from multiple genders and
  races. Register to receive a link to the event one week prior. ABOUT THE 
 BOOK WINNER OF THE PURA BELPRÉ YA AUTHOR AWARD \\* A Morris Award Finalis
 t \\* Parade Best Young Adult Books of All Time \\* Indie Next List Pick \
 \* An unforgettable YA debut about two Latina teens growing up in East Oak
 land as they discover that the world is brimming with messy complexities\,
  perfect for fans of Elizabeth Acevedo and Erika L. Sánchez. Belén Dolor
 es Itzel del Toro wants the normal stuff: to experience love or maybe have
  a boyfriend or at least just lose her virginity. But nothing is normal in
  East Oakland. Her father left her family. She’s at risk of not graduati
 ng. And Leti\, her super-Catholic\, nerdy-ass best friend\, is pregnant—
 by the boyfriend she hasn’t told her parents about\, because he’s Blac
 k\, and her parents are racist. Things are hella complicated. Weighed by a
  depression she can’t seem to shake\, Belén helps Leti\, hangs out with
  an older guy\, and cuts a lot of class. She soon realizes\, though\, that
  distractions are only temporary. Leti is becoming a mother. Classmates ar
 e getting ready for college. But what about Belén? What future is there f
 or girls like her? From debut author Carolina Ixta comes a fierce\, intima
 te examination of friendship\, chosen family\, and the generational cycles
  we must break to become our truest selves. ABOUT THE AUTHOR Carolina Ixta
  is a writer from Oakland\, California. A daughter of Mexican immigrants\,
  she received her BA in creative writing and Spanish language and literatu
 re at the University of California\, Santa Cruz\, and obtained her master'
 s degree in education at the University of California\, Berkeley. Her debu
 t novel\, Shut Up\, This Is Serious\, was a Morris Award finalist\, an LA 
 Times Book Prize finalist\, and the winner of the Pura Belpré Award. Few 
 Blue Skies is her sophomore novel.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1892448265050820/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gian Achen and Clementine Darling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T213000
UID:261018wUhvQGCPHkCPj7LPYREmLQ
DESCRIPTION:Gian Achen is a Bay Area artist whose music blends nostalgic m
 elodies with heartfelt lyrics. Gian's sound is rooted in the golden era of
  '60s rock\, drawing inspiration from iconic bands like The Beatles and Cr
 eedence Clearwater Revival as well as modern artists such as Wilco and The
  Shins. Gian's music invites listeners to join him in a world that’s bot
 h familiar and uniquely his own. Clementine Darling is an Americana Folk S
 inger-Songwriter with her heels dug deep in San Francisco Bay Area’s mus
 ic scene. Originally from Seattle\, Washington\, Darling busked her way do
 wn the West Coast in 2010\, on a road trip that led her to put down roots 
 in Sonoma County\, California. The two locals influenced her debut 11:11 E
 P and subsequent Live At The Lost Church— a collection of introspective 
 songs and soulful ballads\, with undertones of Seattle 90’s grunge. Door
 s Open: 6:30 PM | Show Starts: 7:30 PM
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2181980559421318/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
