BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Let's Cook Messy in Morocco
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T203000
UID:2610312M-EqSGUREuWjduNIerx7g
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, November 13\, 2026 5:30 pm to 8:30 pm\n\nLocation\n\n
 Room 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Arts\n\nExperience Level
 \n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMa
 terials Fee:\n\n$25\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$125\n\nA Moroccan jour
 ney in photographs\, stories\, and a meal we’ll make together.1 · Tea f
 rom a HeightMoroccan mint green tea poured high\, welcoming guests with ph
 otographs and stories from Ryan’s travels.2 · Build the TagineA warming
  fall tagine exploring sweet\, sour\, salty\, and fragrant spices—with p
 reserved lemon bringing everything to life. Option: Chicken or Vegetable. 
 Served with warm Moroccan khobz bread for scooping up the sauce.3 · Roast
 ed Carrots with ChermoulaCaramelized carrots dressed with fresh herbs\, ga
 rlic\, cumin\, lemon\, and olive oil. We’ll make the chermoula together.
 4 · Shlada: Moroccan Tomato SaladFresh tomatoes and cucumber\, chopped wi
 th herbs and a bright lemon-and-olive-oil dressing.5 · Something SweetAlm
 ond ghriba—Moroccan almond cookies\, crackly outside and chewy inside—
 or pears poached with cinnamon\, orange peel\, and cardamom\, a vegan and 
 gluten-free alternative. Served with one last pour of mint tea.Ingredients
  are sourced locally from the Farmers Market\, with a few well-traveled sp
 ices and pantry treasures joining the table. Meal can be made Vegetarians
 /Vegan/Gluten Free upon request\, contact sean@sonomacommunitycenter.org.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/lets-cook-messy-in-morocco/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paint Your Pet’s Portrait: Watercolor for All Levels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T130000
UID:261030lJcbyPGaZUuD6m3C8ESiBA
DESCRIPTION:Fridays Weekly · 3 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nNovember 6 – Nov
 ember 20\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategor
 y\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Leve
 ls\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$225\n\nMaterials Fee:
 \n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$235\n\nChoose a favorite photo of 
 a pet and learn how to render it as a watercolor portrait. Over three week
 s\, you’ll receive instruction from an artist who has painted many commi
 ssioned pet portraits in watercolor. Instructor Hannah Day will share her 
 insights and her approach to rendering animals in this medium\, guiding yo
 u through a layering process that builds vibrancy\, detail\, and depth.Whe
 ther you’re new to watercolor or have experience with the medium\, this 
 class offers an engaging way to develop your skills while creating a perso
 nal portrait of a beloved pet. Your finished painting can be a meaningful 
 keepsake—or a unique holiday gift.You’re welcome to email your photo t
 o us ahead of class\, and we’ll print it for you to use as a reference.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/paint-your-pets-portrait-wa
 tercolor-for-all-levels/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
