UID:261028Bpjfl58KPkGqov1y3lXMjA
DESCRIPTION:Have fun\, enjoy music\, and discover handmade treasures! The 
 Marin County Employee Arts & Crafts Fair returns November 18–19\, from 1
 1 a.m.–4 p.m.\, at the Marin Civic Center cafeteria\, Room 237\, in San 
 Rafael.\n\nShop handcrafts and original art while listening to the County 
 Crows employee band. Different vendors and music each day--visit twice!\n\
 nCraving something sweet? The HR & Friends Bake charity sale and individua
 l bakers sell treats on Wednesday only.\n\nCelebrating its 26th anniversar
 y\, this staff-founded tradition is open to the public. Employees particip
 ate on their own time\, and volunteers in the county's MarinShares program
  provide support. \n\nBrowse original paintings\, drawings\, woodcuts\, a
 nd photographs. Crafts include ceramics\, jewelry\, paper art\, potted pla
 nts\, crocheted dolls\, notecards\, candles\, knitted and crocheted wearab
 les\, and lots more.
LOCATION:Marin County Employee Arts & Crafts Fair
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/marin-county-arts-craft
 s-fair/20282610/2026-11-18T11
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STIMULANT: Art as Remedy for Diseased Culture\, Exhibition and Eve
 nts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T160000
UID:261021H5UWjZdjOkGH63Agdh_Wdw
DESCRIPTION:In a diseased society with failing systems\, what can we do to
  turn things around? For two weeks a new exhibition from Sonoma County’s
  own Apocalypse Studio\, a father and daughter artist duo\, *STIMULANT: A
 rt as Remedy for Diseased Culture* proposes that art is the antidote and 
 creativity is the countermove. This exhibition explores the inner and oute
 r work of co-creating that antidote: art that stimulates society’s creat
 ivity - the social sculpture we all create together. There will be two per
 formances\, two lectures\, a Parisian -style Art Salon\, and times to visi
 t the large exhibition and talk with the artists. All events are free to 
 attend. Visit www.apocalypse.art/stimulant for details and schedule of eve
 nts.
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Guitar Trio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
UID:261020OtfPSIBNfkOTwmleMj4_rA
DESCRIPTION:The universe of guitar knows no boundaries for The California 
 Guitar Trio. Since 1991\, the group has enthralled listeners with a singul
 ar sound that fearlessly crisscrosses genres. The trio’s questing spirit
  drives it to explore the intersections between rock\, jazz\, classical\, 
 and world music. It even throws in the occasional surf or spaghetti Wester
 n tune for good measure. \n\nComprised of Bert Lams\, Hideyo Moriya and Pa
 ul Richards\, the group has established a unique\, personal connection wit
 h audiences. In addition to dazzling musicianship and interplay\, The Cali
 fornia Guitar Trio's \\(CGT\\) shows are full of captivating stories and h
 umor that enable concertgoers to feel like they're part of the music\, not
  just spectators. In fact\, the group’s goal is to transcend their instr
 uments\, so people focus on the music first\, and its considerable technic
 al prowess a distant second. \n\nCGT's 16 albums\, streamed over 65 millio
 n times on Pandora\, offer diverse snapshots of the group’s mercurial mu
 se. The trio’s most recent release Komorebi showcases its acoustic side\
 , with beautiful lush originals and innovative cover arrangements of Beatl
 es\, Beach Boys and more. Other highlights include Masterworks and album o
 f classical works\, with expansive takes on Bach\, Beethoven\, Arvo Pärt\
 , and Schubert. Andromeda\, which combines their many influences into a vi
 sionary album of original material\; CG3\\+2\, an exploration of kinetic r
 ock territory in collaboration with bassist Tony Levin and drummer Pat Mas
 telotto\; and Echoes\, which reimagines timeless material by artists such 
 as Mike Oldfield\, Penguin Café Orchestra\, Pink Floyd\, and Queen. \n\nT
 he trio’s output has made a major global impact\, having served as the s
 oundtrack for Olympics coverage\, and programs on CNN\, CBS\, NBC\, and ES
 PN. They have fans in high places too: Nasa used their music to wake the c
 rew aboard the Space Shuttle Endeavour. \n\nCGT's lineup is truly the sum 
 of its distinct parts: A Utah native now residing in Los Angeles\, Paul Ri
 chards immersed himself in rock\, blues\, jazz\, and folk during his early
  days and while attending The University of Utah’s jazz guitar program. 
 Bert Lams\, originally from Belgium\, graduated from the prestigious Royal
  Conservatory of Music in Brussels\, specializing in classical guitar. Tok
 yo-born Hideyo Moriya began his guitar journey with surf music and British
  rock\, before relocating to Boston to study at Berklee. \n\nAll three fel
 t the call to push themselves to the limit by enrolling in Robert Fripp’
 s challenging Guitar Craft courses\, where they first met in 1987. They we
 nt on to tour together as part of Fripp’s League of Crafty Guitarists\, 
 before forming the California Guitar Trio in Los Angeles four years later.
  \n\nRecently\, the trio expanded its collaborative possibilities by worki
 ng within a six-guitar format with the Montreal Guitar Trio. During these 
 groundbreaking\, highly-entertaining shows\, the acts perform inventive ar
 rangements of each other’s repertoire\, and new music for guitar sextet.
  \n\n30 years and 1\,900\\+ gigs later\, the CGT remains intensely committ
 ed to explore\, evolve and communicate a wide-ranging musical worldview. \
 n\n- By Anil Prasad
LOCATION:Brannan Center
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108287732?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
