UID:2610278VntOFuvEEqHhX7uc32GGQ
DESCRIPTION:Just in time for Thanksgiving\, Chef Charlie Palmer leads a ha
 nds-on master class on the holiday bird at Appellation Healdsburg. Limited
  to ten guests\, the class covers brining for flavor\, breaking down a who
 le turkey\, trussing and roasting it to a caramelized finish\, with every 
 guest working through each step. Winemaker Tom Rochioli pours alongside\, 
 pairing the turkey with the wine he serves at his own Thanksgiving table. 
 Guests leave ready to host the holiday with confidence.
LOCATION:Appellation Healdsburg
URL:https://www.appellationhotels.com/hotels/california-healdsburg/classes
 /turkey-101/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma County Vintners Pour + Explore: Rhône Varietals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T193000
UID:261024M8l3IFxMp0eCQyXc3qtbTA
DESCRIPTION:From rich\, expressive reds to bright\, aromatic whites\, Sono
 ma County’s Rhône varietals offer a world of flavor and character waiti
 ng to be discovered.\n\nJoin us for **Pour + Explore: Rhône Varietals** h
 osted at Longboard Vineyards (5 Fitch Street\, Healdsburg) on Thursday Nov
 ember 19th\, an evening celebrating the diversity\, versatility and distin
 ctive expressions of these beloved grape varieties.\n\n*Participating wine
 ries include Adobe Road Winery\, Anaba Wines\, Bricoleur Vineyards\, Cline
  Family Cellars\, Dutcher Crossing\, Kendric Vineyards\, Lasseter Family W
 ines\, Limerick Lane Cellars\, Longboard Vineyards\, Martinelli Winery\, M
 uscardinni Cellars\, Peay Vineyards\, Pride Mountain Vineyards\, Ram’s G
 ate\, Ridge +MORE!*\n\n***Food available for purchase at event!*** SoCo Pa
 ella brings over 15 years of Spanish cooking experience to Pour & Explore 
 as the event’s exclusive food vendor. Created to complement the host win
 ery’s Rhône wines\, the signature paella features peppery chicken\, ros
 emary-infused pork\, and smoky sausage\, all cooked in fragrant saffron ch
 icken broth with roasted root vegetables.
LOCATION:Longboard Vineyards
URL:https://www.cellarpass.com/events/sonoma-county-vintners-pour-explore-
 rhone-varietals-12459
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T213000
UID:2610236w8y-lIwxUiQMi_vbPF_NQ
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
