SUMMARY:Wreckless Strangers at Rancho Nicasio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:260905ECFlyoYn_EicT1UfBncerg
DESCRIPTION:Fresh off a busy summer of performances across the Bay Area an
 d tour stops in **Littleton\, Colorado**\, and **Jackson Hole\, Wyoming**\
 , **Wreckless Strangers** return this fall with a trio of Northern Califor
 nia shows\, highlighted by an appearance at **Hardly Strictly Bluegrass** 
 in **San Francisco's Golden Gate Park**. The band will also perform at the
  historic **Paper Mill Creek Saloon** in **Forest Knolls** on **September 
 18** and **Rancho Nicasio** on **Friday\, November 20\,** while continuing
  to build momentum with national radio airplay and a climb up the Top 50 A
 mericana and AAA Singles charts.\n\nWith ***Dirty Souls***\, Wreckless Str
 angers return to their rock-and-roll roots\, delivering their rawest and m
 ost visceral studio effort to date. The six-song collection channels the a
 rena rock spirit of the '70s and '80s that shaped the band's earliest infl
 uences while bringing a fresh\, modern edge to the sound. The first single
 \, **"Dirty Soul\,"** continues to receive national airplay and is availab
 le on major streaming platforms. The full album was released in **March**.
 \n\n**Wreckless Stranger**s is a collective of friends and musicians carry
 ing the torch for San Francisco’s grand rock ‘n’ roll tradition. The
 ir unique blend of “Ameri-Cali Soul” melds the contemporary blues styl
 ings of Bonnie Raitt and Boz Scaggs\; the songwriting sensibilities of Son
 s of Champlin and Fleetwood Mac\; the swashbuckling Americana of the Lost 
 Planet Airmen and Peter Rowan\; and the funk of Sly Stone and Tower of Pow
 er with a dash of Grateful Dead and Jefferson Airplane for flavor and unpr
 edictability. With soaring vocal harmonies and burning instrumental improv
 isation\, framed by concise\, poignant original songwriting\, Wreckless St
 rangers seek to honor and carry forth the brand of free-spirited musical f
 un and adventure that defines the Bay Area. \n\nThe band features **Amber
  Morris** on lead vocals\; **David Noble** on lead guitar and lead vocals\
 ; **Joshua Zucker** on bass and vocals\; **Mick Hellman** on drums and voc
 als\; **Rob Anderson** on guitar and vocals\; and **Fletcher Nielsen** on 
 keys. \n\n***Dirty Souls*** is the band’s third studio outing under the
  tutelage of Grammy-winning producer **Dave Way**\, who fosters a level of
  depth and organic cohesion that firmly establishes Wreckless Strangers in
  San Francisco’s storied rock ’n’ roll legacy. The songwriting is am
 ong their most intimate and personal\, exploring themes of relationships\,
  loss\, empowerment\, and perseverance. Co-lead singers **Amber Morris** a
 nd **David Noble** function as a single organism\, bringing the songs to l
 ife with bluesy grit\, soul\, and humanity bolstered by rock-solid\, road-
 hewn grooves.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:http://ranchonicasio.com/events/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
