SUMMARY:Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:261031JidpFAZJREmrd89mslQmZw
DESCRIPTION:C Major Moods\n\nJoint Concert featuring the Sonoma State Symp
 hony Orchestra \\(Alexander Kahn\, Music Director\\) and the Santa Rosa Sy
 mphony Young People's Chamber Orchestra\\(Aaron Westman\, Music Director\\
 )\n\nPlease join us for an evening of two remarkable symphonies from the e
 arly nineteenth century\, both of which are in the key of C!\n\nThis conce
 rt is a collaboration between the Sonoma State Symphony Orchestra and the 
 Santa Rosa Symphony Young People's Chamber Orchestra\, who will join force
 s throughout the program.\n\nOn the first half of the program is the passi
 onate and virtuousic Symphony no. 1 from 1847 by Emile Mayer\, the most pr
 olific female composer active in Germany during the 19th century. After th
 e intermission we bring you Beethoven's ground-breaking Symphony No. 1 \\(
 1800\\)\, the symphony that launched the Romantic period and put Beethoven
 's name on the map as a symphonist. The Beethoven will be performed withou
 t a conductor\, led from the violin by SSU violin/viola faculty member and
  YPCO Music Director Aaron Westman.
LOCATION:Green Music Center - Weill Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-2?utm_source=sonoma
 _calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orche
 stra_nov20
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
