DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T123000
UID:261023M7gnhP8V1EuXiTcRk1BN3w
DESCRIPTION:Susan Topf’s Yoga Hike balances a mix of easy hiking and gen
 tle yoga postures\, breath work and guided meditation\, no mat necessary. 
 The route varies on weather conditions and group interest\, typically cove
 ring 2-3 miles of varied terrain. All levels and ages welcome.\n\nTickets 
 are $20. Please wear weather-appropriate clothing to feel comfortable bein
 g in a natural setting and bring water (as needed). Meet outside the Visit
 or Center unless otherwise noted in the reminder email prior to the hike. 
 Limited to 12 participants. \n\nSonoma County Resident? Free with a Septe
 mber 2026 or newer Park Rx from a participating Sonoma County Medical Prov
 ider. To sign up with a Park Rx\, please forward a PDF of your signed Rx t
 o alma@sonomaecologycenter.org for a sign up code.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026yoga-hikes
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
UID:261023F5pWTcLCD0yYzdD4-W3Ggw
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers 2026 Holiday Book & Craft Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T133000
UID:261022dp9f1LoaMUuuNOkAwGuisQ
DESCRIPTION:Redwood Writers 2026 Holiday Book & Craft Fair\n\nNovember 21\
 , 2026\, 11 a.m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa FREE!\n\nJoin us on Saturday\
 , November 21\, from 11 a.m. to 1:30 p.m. in Room 5 \\(Senior Wing\\) at t
 he Finley Center for our 3rd Annual Holiday Party and Book & Craft Fair! T
 his lively\, event brings together local authors and crafters\, offering b
 ooks and handmade treasures that make perfect holiday gifts for yourself o
 r your loved ones. Admission is FREE so that you can find the perfect loca
 l gift for your loved ones. The afternoon will be a celebration among frie
 nds\, delicious food\, and creative gifts made by local artisans and autho
 rs.\n\nMembers\, please bring a savory or sweet dish to share for our potl
 uck\, if you can!\n\nMark your calendars and plan to join us for a joyful 
 afternoon of shopping\, mingling\, and celebrating creativity in our commu
 nity.\n\nA chance to meet nice people with cool crafts\, books\, and other
  helpful services for creative souls and writers:\n\nMalena Eljumaily \\(C
 rafts\\): Knitted and crocheted items\, plus other handcrafts\n\nTaylor Me
 tzler \\(Books & Crafts\\): Books\, chainmaille jewelry\, crocheted items\
 n\nPamela Heck \\(Books & Art\\)\n\nRedwood Writers \\(Books\\): Redwood W
 riters anthologies and swag\n\nPatricia L. Morin \\(Books\\): Psychologica
 l paranormal thriller Moloch and the Angel\; short story collections Myste
 ry Montage\, Crime Montage\, Confetti\, Deadly Illusions\n\nStacey Dennick
  \\(Other\\): Comic zines\, plus info on SRJC’s free Lifelong Learning c
 lasses\n\nCrissi Langwell \\(Books & Art\\): Romance books and art\n\nShaw
 n Langwell \\(Books and Marketing Consulting\\): Personal growth and inspi
 rational books helping authors move past the mental obstacles of putting t
 heir work into the world\n\nN.E. White \\(Books\\): Mapmaker Books 1–3\;
  The Legend of Damndrake and The Rescue of Damndrake \\(epic fantasy with 
 dragons\\)\n\nJanet Henker \\(Books\\): Two novels and an anthology\, plus
  baked goods\n\nLaura McHale Holland \\(Books\\): Novels\, short story col
 lections\, memoirs\n\nSarah Paris \\(Books\\): Haiku and magic realism nov
 ellas\n\nNatalie Gould \\(Books\\): Memoir\, plus crafts \\(dried flower w
 reaths\, paintings\, cards\\)\n\nLisa Manterfield \\(Books\\): Mystery/sus
 pense novels A Strange Companion\, The Smallest Thing\, All Our Lies Are T
 rue\n\nDawn Dolan \\(Books\\): Two children’s books with matching merch 
 \\(mugs\, thermoses\, plushies\\)\n\nKen Berman \\(Books\\): Books\, magne
 ts\, and character merch\n\nBrian Martens \\(Books & Art\\): Poetry books 
 Three Raven Gate and Merlin’s Wing\, plus small paintings\n\nNeil Burgst
 ahler \\(Books\\)\n\nJoan Tabb \\(Books\\)\n\nTessa Burns \\(Books\\)
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/redwood-writers-2026-holiday-book-craft-fai
 r/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
