BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Les Claypool
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T160000
UID:261031-taGdbFk9kGO24jk3y3Exg
DESCRIPTION:Leslie Edward &quot\;Les&quot\; Claypool is a bassist and lead
  singer\, best known for his work with the alternative rock band Primus. B
 orn on September 29\, 1963\, in Richmond\, California\, Claypool's mastery
  of the electric bass has brought him into the spotlight with his funky\, 
 creative playing style. Though he cites bass virtuoso Geddy Lee of Rush\, 
 and the experimental group The Residents as his greatest influence\, Clayp
 ool is known to use various styles in his playing\, Claypool mixes finger-
 tapping\, flamenco-like strumming\, and a Larry Graham-like slap technique
  to develop his own unique style.  Claypool has earned respect as one of R
 ock's premier bass talents and has become an influence on younger bassists
  in recent years. He has played with other artists such as Tom Waits and B
 uckethead.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040621527?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petite Landscapes in Acrylic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
UID:261030wP3loV8wHUit6Zi2PpVrBg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 10:00 am to 2:00 pm\n\nLocation\
 n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nExperience Le
 vel\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$65\n\nM
 aterials Fee:\n\n$20\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$85\n\nHave you always
  wanted to paint landscapes but don’t know where to start? Or are you cu
 rious about acrylics but haven’t taken the plunge yet? In this class\, y
 ou’ll learn a simple technique to create small\, abstract landscapes on 
 5” square wooden tiles using a limited palette of colors.You’ll be gui
 ded through the basics of acrylic paints and mediums\, including surface p
 reparation\, color blending with a flat bristle brush\, and using differen
 t tools to add texture and detail. By the end of the class\, you’ll appl
 y a final coat of medium to seal and protect your artwork\, leaving you wi
 th 2-3 completed pieces to take home\, along with a little easel to displa
 y your favorite one.This class is perfect for beginners\, though some prio
 r painting experience is helpful. The process you’ll learn can easily be
  applied to larger paintings or even collage projects.All materials are pr
 ovided. Feel free to bring snacks or a bag lunch to eat while you work.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/petite-landscapes-in-acryli
 c-112126/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:November Soda Club Firing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T170000
UID:261030s5JodPD2KE-DMaQWskuQlg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, Sunday\, and Wednesday\n\nDates & Times\n\nSaturday
 \, November 21\, 2026 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM\n\nSunday\, November 22\, 2026 
 10:00 AM – 6:00 PM \\*Time is subject to change\n\nWednesday\, November 
 25\, 2026\n\n\\*unload date subject to change based on club consensus 4:00
  Pm – 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nKiln Shed\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Worksho
 ps\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advanced\n\nAges\n\n17+\n\nRegi
 stration Cost:\n\n$110\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$15\n\nTotal Registration Cost
 :\n\n$125 **Prerequisites to enroll in Soda Firing Club**:\n\nMust have ta
 ken at least one\, Intro to Mid-Range Soda Firing Workshop\n\nBe well vers
 ed in protocols for loading the soda kiln\, kiln safety\, equipment and op
 erating safety\, and be willing and able to be unsupervised with the kiln 
 during loading\, unloading\, and post firing cleaning of the kiln.\n\nMust
  have pre-approval from the Director of Ceramics or Soda Club Facilitator\
 n\n**program overview**\n\nThe “Julia” Soda Firing Club is designed fo
 r folks looking for longterm use with our Soda Kiln\, Julia. The club is l
 ed by Studio Monitors\, and a Studio Technician but involves no formal ins
 truction in soda firing processes. Without a formalized instructor\, our S
 oda Club offers a more financially accessible way of having work soda-fire
 d\, without the need to retake our Intro to Soda Firing workshop courses. 
 The Soda Club will run firings monthly or as often as desired and needed d
 epending on participant interest. Unlike our Soda Firing Workshops\, club 
 firings will include no instruction on wadding\, slips\, glazes\, or any l
 ectures on the subject of soda firing. As such\, participants must feel co
 mfortable with the safety and care of the equipment\, as well as loading\,
  firing\, and maintenance procedures surrounding the firing process. **Eac
 h participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. (Tip\; Make sure all your
  pots fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot of space).
 (Tip\; Make sure all your pots fit approximately into a milk crate which i
 s 1 cubic foot of space).**
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/november-soda-club-firing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
