BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Native Beat: Native American Music of Sonoma County
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T153000
UID:2608304PfFLOJD80WYFT6KYwwcfA
DESCRIPTION:Professor Paul Steward presents a lecture and performance of N
 ative American music from local tribal cultures\, and a selection of diffe
 rent tribal cultures across the USA. Paul Steward is an accomplished educa
 tor\, professional musician\, and enrolled tribal member of the Elem India
 n Colony of Pomo Indians. Serving as a Lecturer in Native American and Ame
 rican Indian Studies at San Francisco State University and Sonoma State Un
 iversity since 2016\, he specializes in California Indian history\, cultur
 e\, and tribal relations. Parallel to his academic career\, Steward is a c
 elebrated singer\, songwriter\, and guitarist with over 20 years of profes
 sional experience. By uniquely blending traditional Pomo rhythms\, languag
 e\, and instruments with modern blues and soul\, his work creates a vital 
 cultural bridge that has earned him prestigious accolades\, including the 
 Native American Music Awards and recognition as a Yerba Buena Center for t
 he Arts honoree.
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/native-beat-native-american-mus
 ic-sonoma-county
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:UC Master Gardeners: All About Growing Beautiful Orchids
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T120000
UID:260820eOkbU6_F7ECSvzDFPMdtrQ
DESCRIPTION:Orchids are the largest family of flowering plants in the worl
 d\, with over 25\,000 species found in nature\, and probably in the order 
 of 150\,000 different hybrids. Many think orchids are difficult to grow\, 
 but with some basic information\, anyone can be successful with growing or
 chids. This presentation will cover: Understanding the basic needs and car
 e for growing most orchids at home. An introduction to the more common orc
 hid groups that are possible to grow. Learning which types can grow outsid
 e on the Sonoma Coast. Registration Encouraged: Visit Upcoming Events to c
 omplete your registration. After registering\, you will receive a confirma
 tion email containing information about attending the library talk. Learn 
 about home gardening\, pest management\, water conservation practices\, an
 d more from your Sonoma County UC Master Gardeners! Different presentation
  topic per location.
LOCATION:Northwest Santa Rosa Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/uc-master-gardeners-all-about-g
 rowing-beautiful-orchids-117790
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
