BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Endless Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T180000
UID:261014butFwj9gvEaDVOSyouCTtA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  10/12/26\n\n**NOVEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 ENDLESS INSPIRATION**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– October 26  – November 22\
 , 2026**\n\n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, November 7\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to
  meet Ron Sumner and Karen Miller and learn about their art and inspiratio
 n.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a 
 beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSo
 noma County artist\, **Ron Sumner\,** presents **Endless Inspiration**\, a
  collection of new paintings and classic works that highlight his lifelong
  love of nature featuring landscapes\, animals and wildlife\, with a speci
 al focus on birds.  The essence of this golden state shines forth in “C
 alifornia Hills\,” a large oil painting of a sweep of oak covered hills.
    Turning to wildlife\, Sumner’s masterful watercolor rendition in th
 e “Young Fox” captures its wild nature on stark alert.  And the compe
 lling presence of a most majestic bird is beautifully memorialized in his 
 “Blue Heron” watercolor.  Other birds depicted in his works include p
 arrots\, penguins and owls.  “In my painting\, I always strive to trans
 late my emotional response to the world of nature around us – to share t
 his deep feeling with those who view my work\,” commented Sumner on his 
 inspiration.\n\nA lifelong Northern Californian\, Sumner began his art tra
 ining in school.  After earning a BFA from the California College of Arts
  & Crafts\, he was a technical illustrator for a number of years before tr
 ansitioning to a full-time fine arts painter.  With an emphasis in waterc
 olor\, he has won numerous awards\, including Best of Show at the Society 
 of Western Artists.  His portrait of John F. Kennedy is part of the perma
 nent collection at the John F. Kennedy Library.  He has exhibited widely 
 and was part of the Veterans Art Show for CA vets in 2023.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Sumner will co-host Art Nite on 11/5 from 5 pm to 7 pm.\n\nThe Stairw
 ay Smallworks Showcase features **Karen Miller’**s **Historic Gems\,** f
 eaturing pastel paintings that honor our history – local artifacts that 
 are disappearing.  Highlighting this exhibit\, “Ghost Bridge\,” an ea
 rly 20th century railroad bridge known as Healdsburg Railroad Bridge is so
 on to give way for the Smart Train.  Its unique style is a key element to
  our local character but sadly could not be upgraded for modern rail.  Fr
 om old trucks to a beloved schoolhouse\, these paintings harken fond memor
 ies.  Part of our world for years\, they enriched our lives and are not t
 o be forgotten.  Noted Miller on the impetus for her series\, “I want t
 o catch old things before they’re gone – memorializing those things cl
 ose to our hearts.”\n\nMeet the artist: Miller will host the Gallery on 
 October 26 and November 2\, 11\, 14 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n Also j
 oin us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, November 5\, 5 – 7 pm. 
  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a communi
 ty event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participati
 ng.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\,
  Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    
 **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beve
 rly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa Valley College Chorale - "A Hero's Journey"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T151500
UID:261013dOiLv_sCSUiCNgbvURxskg
DESCRIPTION:Every story worth telling begins the same way. Not with a plan
 . Not with a hero who is ready. \n\nIt begins with a call. \n\nJoseph Ca
 mpbell found the same journey running beneath human stories across every c
 ulture and every century: the ordinary life disrupted\, the threshold cros
 sed\, the road that takes everything\, the transformation that finally mak
 es the return possible. \n\n*A Hero’s Journey* is a choral concert bui
 lt on that arc. Five movements. One story. Music spanning Vivaldi to Rodge
 rs and Hammerstein\, a forgotten inscription on a cellar wall in wartime C
 ologne\, a Broadway meditation on hope written for a daughter\, ancient li
 turgy\, and a 21st-century voice asking\, quietly\, what it costs to get d
 ressed and show up. Between movements\, students from the NVC Reader’s T
 heater class give voice to the arc — narrating the journey from call to 
 return. \n\nThe NVC Chorale invites you to make the journey with them —
  a concert about the rest of us. The ones who weren’t ready. The ones 
 who went anyway.
LOCATION:Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Matt Bradford
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T150000
UID:261010jhoXtp94Ak2jK4AsbDiHeA
DESCRIPTION:Combining blistering dobro and gritty lyrics\, Matt Bradford w
 eaves instrumental mastery and heartfelt songwriting into a genre-defying 
 blend of Folk\, Blues\, Americana\, Country\, and Pop. The savvy listener 
 will detect echoes of a wide range of artists from Townes Van Zandt to Bru
 ce Springsteen\, and Jeffrey Foucault to Chris Whitley. But ultimately\, i
 t is distinctly Matt Bradford. Matt's music is available on itunes and spo
 tify. https://itunes.apple.com/us/artist/matt-bradford/id552581869
LOCATION:Moonlight Brewing Company
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108597053?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lucy Kaplansky
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T180000
UID:260910tDj85AOxsUmmYjmbKJ9C6A
DESCRIPTION:Lucy Kaplansky \\(born 1960\\) is a folk musician based in New
  York City. \n\n Originally from Chicago\, at the age of 18\, moved to New
  York City where she became involved in the city's Greenwich Village folk 
 music scene.\n\n \n\n In 1983\, she decided to become a psychologist\, enr
 olling in Yeshiva University. She continued playing music while doing her 
 PhD\, and began to have some success as part of a duo with Shawn Colvin. H
 owever\, when they began to attract record company interest\, Kaplansky de
 clined\, choosing instead to set up a private practice and become a staff 
 psychologist at a New York hospital. For several years\, she concentrated 
 largely on her work\, and played little in the way of concerts. However\, 
 she still did some session work\, such as singing backing vocals in the st
 udio for Suzanne Vega.\n\n \n\n By the early 1990s she found herself incre
 asingly drawn back to music. Colvin\, who by this time had experienced som
 e commercial success\, offered to produce an album for her. The result\, T
 he Tide\, a mixture of her own songs and several covers\, was released by 
 Red House Records \\(Greg Brown's label\\) in 1994. At this time\, she dec
 ided to give up her psychology practice\, and return to music full-time. S
 he released her second album\, \\[album artist=Lucy Kaplansky\\]Flesh and 
 Bone\, in 1996.\n\n \n\n In 1998 Kaplansky joined with Dar Williams and Ri
 chard Shindell to form the folk group Cry Cry Cry\, which made an album an
 d toured extensively resulting from the success of the originally planned 
 six week tour. \n\n \n\n 1999's Ten Year Night won rave reviews and booste
 d her popularity\, leading to performances on CBS-TV. \n\n She followed th
 at album with Every Single Day which was released in 2001.\n\n \n\n The Re
 d Thread\, released in early 2004\, includes songs about adopting her new 
 daughter Molly\, who Lucy and her husband Rick brought home from China in 
 late 2003\, and several songs relating to her experiences living in downto
 wn Manhattan during 9-11. A new album is to be released in March of 2007.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108207770?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
