DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T160000
UID:260629-DfVoQpcGUSch6bOzhWklw
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma's 10th Annual Holiday Food Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T200000
UID:261028-gYxRnZcq0GBh18GvQJlBg
DESCRIPTION:Mon Nov 23rd 3:00-8:00 An Indoor Farmer's Market - Purchase Di
 rectly From Local Artisans & Prepare for the Holidays!\n\nholidayfoodfair.
 com for a list of vendors\n\nMon Nov 23rd 3:00 to 8:00: \\(The Monday befo
 re Thanksgiving\\) The Petaluma Holiday Food Fair is an indoor farmer’s 
 market where folks can purchase directly from local food artisans to prepa
 re for thanksgiving and beyond. This year\, for the first time\, we are ho
 sting our annual event at our distillery \\(Barber Lee Spirits\\) in downt
 own Petaluma\, where fair attendees will also have the opportunity to tast
 e our spirits and enjoy seasonal cocktails and libations while they shop a
 nd enjoy our extensive holiday decorations!\n\nFREE tickets and reservatio
 ns are required\, and will book your timeslot for entry.\n\nKids do not r
 equire tickets.\n\nAfter the 2017 wildfires devastated Sonoma County\, Lor
 raine & Michael Barber of the Brutal Hill Winery noticed that many of the 
 local artisans they supported in their tasting room were suffering from la
 ck of business. At the height of harvest season\, farmers markets were clo
 sed and sales were slim. They organized this event to get a much needed fi
 nancial boost to local food producers. The event has become a vital start 
 to the holiday season and remains an important and beloved event for local
  food artisans and Sonoma County residents to kick off the holiday season!
 \n\nSampling is up to the discretion of the individual vendors. Beer\, Win
 e\, Cocktails\, and Non-Alcoholic drinks will be available for consumption
  onsite. The number of people allowed in at one time is limited. Tickets a
 re free and include a time preference \\(15 minute increments\\) so there
 ’s less of a wait and some more space. Kids do not require tickets!
LOCATION:Barber Lee Spirits
URL:http://holidayfoodfair.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
