BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Janice Gould's This Music: Record of a Poet Becoming
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T190000
UID:260819YfFQT5zSZk-A6brDIsrjnQ
DESCRIPTION:Two of the book's editors-Kim Shuck \\(Cherokee\\)\, former Sa
 n Francisco Poet Laureate\, essayist and fiber artist\; and Jennifer Foers
 ter \\(Mvskoke\\)\, published poet\, arts administrator\, and professor-pr
 esent this many-layered work. This Music is a vital contribution to Indige
 nous and LGBTQ\\+ literatures\, offering readers a rare and powerful accou
 nt of gender\, sexuality\, and Native identity in mid-century and contempo
 rary America. This work honors Gould's legacy while expanding the canon of
  poetic memoir. Ideal for readers of poetry\, memoir\, and Indigenous lite
 rature\, this book will resonate deeply with anyone drawn to stories of re
 silience\, creativity\, and the enduring power of memory. Other editors of
 This Musicare Deborah Miranda\, enrolled Ohlone\, poet\, and author of the
  iconicBad Indians: A Tribal Memoir\; Lisa Tatonetti\, Kansas State Univer
 sity professor and author\; and Marie-Elise Wheatwind. This Music is from 
 the is from the  University of Arizona Press .
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/janice-goulds-this-music-record-of-a-
 poet-becoming/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T170000
UID:261004b3N3TTb9xEOYmqLuW6afqw
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T170000
UID:260914Zg3XRJoclkuafrwhflRLEg
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
