BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:13th Annual Post-Thanksgiving Turkey Waddle Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261127T123000
UID:261029DApYaFLhJked9CFWLUX2nQ
DESCRIPTION:Jack London State Historic Park’s annual Turkey Waddle Hike 
 lets everyone get out and “shake their tail feathers” after a day of f
 easting and football.   Celebrated on the day after Thanksgiving since 2
 014\, this moderate 3.5-mile round trip hike leads through mixed evergreen
 s on the way to the majestic Ancient Redwood \\(also affectionately known 
 as the Grandmother Tree\\).\n\n Great for all ages\, “waddlers” shoul
 d wear sturdy shoes and bring water.  The trail includes uneven and rocky
  surfaces and involves some elevation gain and loss.  The event will be c
 ancelled in the event of rain. \n\n Tickets are $15 per person \\(the pa
 rk entry fee is waived\\).   Reservations and more information are avail
 able at https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/turkey-waddle-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
