UID:261012jVN04eF_ak2zmk7LwJO4nA
DESCRIPTION:Join our Docents on this fun family hike that is good for all 
 ages\, where you will learn about Sugarloaf Park\, its plants\, animals\, 
 and history. \n\nThe hike begins from the Visitor Center. One option head
 s down to the waterfall on the 2-mile Pony Gate-Canyon loop\, while a seco
 nd\, shorter option will meander along the Creekside Nature Trail. Please 
 note the route is bound to change depending on logistics such as wet cross
 ings and the participants' physical ability. Free event\, RSVP required. W
 ear layers\, appropriate footwear for slippery/rocky trails\, bring at lea
 st 32oz of water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees
  apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026greenfriday
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
