UID:260801yqzt-nbZxEaqiQ6U0ur0UQ
DESCRIPTION:Relive the 70s when Tower of Power returns to the LBC on Satur
 day\, November 28! For 58 years\, Tower of Power has delivered the best in
  funk and soul music. Once East Bay Grease defined their sound\, the 70s w
 ere a boom period for the band with radio classics like “So Very Hard to
  Go” and “What Is Hip?” They continued to tour and record over the y
 ears\, returning to Oakland in 2018 for their 50th anniversary. They’ve 
 travelled the world\, enjoying hit singles on their own and backing legend
 ary artists\, including Otis Redding\, Elton John\, Santana\, the Grateful
  Dead\, John Lee Hooker\, Aerosmith\, Bonnie Raitt\, and countless others.
  In the process they’ve defined the instantly recognizable “Oakland so
 ul” sound.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/tower-of-power-26/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
