BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Women of Jack London's Beauty Ranch: Hands That Shaped the Vis
 ion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261129T120000
UID:261028nJa5F4CiNkydTBV-jrY1ng
DESCRIPTION:In honor of Charmian London’s birthday on November 27\, join
  a walk celebrating her legacy and recognizing the many women whose lives\
 , work\, and creativity have helped shape the history\, culture\, and land
 scape of the park.\n\nIn the five short years Jack London lived at Beauty 
 Ranch\, he imagined it on a grand scale. That vision took root and endured
  through the labor\, intelligence\, and perseverance of two key women\, Ch
 armian Kittredge London and Eliza Shepard — who stewarded the dream\, la
 nd\, and legacy through upheaval and change\, long after Jack London was g
 one. This two-hour tour of Beauty Ranch and the House of Happy Walls Museu
 m invites visitors to step into their stories and discover how a vision be
 came an enduring reality.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-women-of-beauty-ranch-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
